-- title:
--   Level-N Brandt count equals enhanced supersingular ℓ-isogeny count
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of prime characteristic $q'$, algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, let $X_1$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose $q'$-torsion is trivial, and let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy $a<0$, $b<0$ and: for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice that is an order (containing $1$, multiplicatively closed, finitely generated, $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning) and maximal among orders containing it, and let $\theta_1$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the subring of $\operatorname{End}(X_1(\kappa))$ generated by the rational homomorphisms $X_1\to X_1$ onto $\Lambda_1$. Let $N\ge 1$ with $q'\nmid N$, and let $m$ be an adelic unit with $m$ and $N\cdot m^{-1}$ in the box $\widehat{\Lambda_1}$ of $\Lambda_1$, such that the conjugate lattice $m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}\cap\mathbb{H}$ is again a maximal order; put $R=\Lambda_1\cap(m\widehat{\Lambda_1}m^{-1}\cap\mathbb{H})$ and assume $R$ has index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\ne q'$ and $\ell\nmid N$. Finally let $x,y$ be adelic units equipped with level-$N$ kernel-ideal realisations: for $x$, an elliptic curve $W_x$, a nonzero rational homomorphism $\chi_x:X_1\to W_x$ and a unit $d_x\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^\times$ with $\theta_1$ carrying $\{\rho\circ\chi_x:\rho:W_x\to X_1\text{ rational}\}$ onto $\overline{d_x\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda_1})}$, an elliptic curve $W_x'$ and rational maps $\psi_x:W_x\to W_x'$, $\psi_x':W_x'\to W_x$ with $\psi_x'\circ\psi_x=N$ and $\psi_x\circ\psi_x'=N$, such that $\ker\psi_x$ is cyclic of order $N$ and $\theta_1$ carries $\{\rho\circ(\psi_x\circ\chi_x)\}$ onto $\overline{d_x\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap xm\widehat{\Lambda_1})}$; and the same data $W_y,\chi_y,d_y,W_y',\psi_y,\psi_y'$ for $y$. Then the number of $\mathbb{Z}$-lattices $J\subseteq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ that are simultaneously of the form $\mathbb{H}\cap xh\widehat{R}$ for some adelic unit $h$ lying in $\widehat{R}$ with $\ell h^{-1}\in\widehat{R}$ but $h^{-1}\notin\widehat{R}$ and $\ell^{-1}h\notin\widehat{R}$, and of the form $c\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap y\widehat{R})$ for some $c\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^\times$, equals the number of subgroups $D\le W_x(\kappa)$ of order $\ell$ for which there are rational homomorphisms $\varphi:W_x\to W_y$ and $\varphi':W_y\to W_x$ with $\ker\varphi=D$, $\varphi'\circ\varphi=\ell$, $\varphi\circ\varphi'=\ell$ and $\varphi(\ker\psi_x)\subseteq\ker\psi_y$.
--
--   This is the good-prime entry-by-entry comparison in Eichler's dictionary between quaternionic class sets with Eichler level structure and supersingular elliptic curves with level-$N$ structure: for $\ell$ prime to $Nq'$, the Brandt-matrix entry counting right $R$-lattice steps at $\ell$ from the class of $x$ to the class of $y$ agrees with the supersingular Hecke-operator entry counting $\ell$-isogenies of the enhanced curves $(W_x,\ker\psi_x)$ and $(W_y,\ker\psi_y)$. It is used in the identification of the supersingular Hecke matrix with the class-set Hecke matrix at primes of good reduction.
